// us.irs.rev_rul_afr — the IRS Revenue Rulings publishing the Applicable
// Federal Rates (AFR) of 26 U.S.C. §1274(d) and the related tables.
//
// WHY A PACKAGE. Four `afr_rates` rows of GAPS-INVENTORY (§453(l)(3),
// §7872(f)(2)(B), §167(g)(2), §860E(c)(2)) read a rate(short|mid|long,
// semiannual, month T) from the §1274(d) tables, published as monthly
// Revenue Rulings. No row names concrete months: owners need the table
// contract «rate(horizon, compounding, month) → figure» plus anchored months,
// not the 2000–2026 archive. One issue's Table 1 carries all three horizons
// (short/mid/long-term AFR, annual/semiannual/quarterly/monthly); the second
// issue proves month-keyed lookup and parser stability.
//
// WHAT IT HOLDS (phase 1 + Table 3, still rule-less). `sources/rr-26-*.pdf`
// — the official IRS bytes, pinned by sha256 (`sources/provenance.json`:
// URL, bytes, sha256, last-modified, issue, table inventory — no rate
// values). `sources.law` + `sources/tables/afr-2026-*.lawtable.json` —
// Table 1 of each issue as structure (3 × 56 rows) with quote-anchored
// fragments, plus `month-index.json` (month → ruling/table/edition), plus
// `sources/tables/afr-382-2026-*.lawtable.json` — Table 3 of each issue
// (§382(f): adjusted federal long-term rate + long-term tax-exempt rate,
// 3 × 2 rows, one `AFR_2026_*_T3` fragment per issue, `table382` per month
// in month-index under the same selection policy). All of it GENERATED by
// `corpus/tools/sources/sync/sync_us_irs_afr_rulings.py`, never hand-edited.
// No rules: the value, its window and its reading belong to the owner, the
// rate entering the case as a case fact (`afr_semiannual_for_year`). Same
// shape as `us.irc.inflation_adjustments`.
//
// LAYOUT NOTE. `check_laws_tree` §3.5 derives `us/rev-rul-afr` from
// jurisdiction US + instrument guidance (`us.irs` is not a GROUP_BY_NAME_PREFIX
// group): the package name keeps the `irs` issuer segment, the path does not.
//
// OUT OF SCOPE. The quarterly §6621 series (sibling candidate
// `us.irs.rev_rul_6621_*`, e.g. Rev. Rul. 2026-15); Rev. Proc. 2024-40/2025-32
// (already in `us.irc.inflation_adjustments`).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package us.irs.rev_rul_afr version "0.1.1";
namespace "urn:us:irs:rev_rul_afr:clir";
